 ## Background
-The method is part of the Legolizer system, introduced in 2009 by [S1]. It was developed to create LEGO representations from boundary models in real-time. The approach differs from earlier methods by Karabassi et al. and Passalis et al., which used six z-buffers and six passes, by utilizing a single render pass and buffer [S1]. The method relies on mesh subdivision to ensure vertices sample the surface well, allowing the image-space projection to create a good volumetric approximation [S1].
